  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">&#160;</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">&#160;</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></math> be twice differentiable functions such that <math><msup> <mi>f</mi> <mo>&#8243;</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;and <math><msup> <mi>g</mi> <mo>&#8243;</mo> </msup></math>&nbsp;are continuous functions on <math><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></math> . Suppose <math> <mrow> <msup> <mi>f</mi> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msup> <mi>f</mi> <mo>&#8243;</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> and <math><msup> <mi>g</mi> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0.</mn><munder> <mrow> <mi>lim</mi> </mrow> <mrow> <mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn> </mrow> </munder> <mfrac> <mrow> <mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow> </mrow> <mrow> <msup> <mi>f</mi> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup><mi>&#160;</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>&#160;</mi><msup> <mi>g</mi> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo> </math> then",
